      <Value Culture="en-us"><![CDATA[{
  "name": "1 column layout",
  "sections": [
    {
      "grid": "12",
      "rows": [
        {
          "name": "Article 8 + 4",
          "id": "4006b498-519a-41be-ad31-1325646ee4cf",
          "areas": [
            {
              "grid": "8",
              "controls": [
                {
                  "value": "<p>I've been a passionate developer since I got my first computer when I was 16.<br />Without knowing what significance this machine would one day have, I was immediately fascinated when my best friend showed me his first Sinclair.<br />My first should then be a Sinclair ZX Spectrum. I wanted to understand how a computer works and dealt equally with hardware and software. For months I had been working on a hardware interface and associated software in assembler to control a plotter that I had also built myself.<br />The mechanics of the plotter had overtaxed my skills, but the interface and software were functional.</p>\n<p>So it would have been only too obvious to study electrical engineering after my Abitur (major subjects: math and physics). Since life doesn't run according to rational criteria, I finally studied graphic design with a focus on illustration and typography and graduated in 1991 with a diploma.</p>\n<p>In 1991, the computer was already conquering the graphics industry and my first employer dealt exclusively with desktop publishing. From then on, the computer was part of my daily work routine. I came to internet programming in 1997 via the intermediate step of multimedia programming with Macromedia's director.</p>\n<p>Since 2009 I have been developing Content Management System based websites, preferably with Umbraco CMS.</p>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": "rte"
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                }
              ],
              "styles": null,
              "config": null
